<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Apart from the surplus currently existing, next fortnight is expected to see a net deficit in excess of 16,000 million rupees for the banking system. The double impact of advance tax outflows and the seven year gilt auction will put upward pressure on overnight rates, and, some correction in prices of government securities is very likely. Most of the outflows are in the beginning of the fortnight and subsequently intervention by RBI in the forex markets and termination of the strike by SBI could ease pressure on rates towards month end.</p>
